 "text": "You run a warehouse in Tampa. A hurricane watch just went up. Forecasters issue those about 48 hours before tropical storm winds arrive. You have 3,000 orders waiting to ship. You get one move. Option A. Run every shift and ship as many orders as you can before the storm. Option B. Stop shipping now, move stock off the floor, and send your people home to prepare. Comment A or B. Part 2 shows what the storm does to each choice."
